title: 'staking-async: check inactivity per service in chill_inactive'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `IsValidatorInactive::is_inactive` now receives the era points of the validator per
    `ServiceKind`, as `&[(ServiceKind, RewardPoint)]`, instead of a single total.
    A runtime can so decide inactivity per service, for example that only relay consensus points
    keep a validator active.

    Points of the tally not recorded per service, which are those of eras before points were
    recorded per service, count as `RelayConsensus`. A service the validator earned nothing for may
    be missing from the slice.

    `chill_inactive` is now disabled by default:
    - The `()` implementation of `IsValidatorInactive` never finds a validator inactive. The new
      `AllZero` implementation has the old behaviour of `()`: a validator is inactive if it earned
      no points for any service. Runtimes that want the old behaviour must use `AllZero`. Custom
      implementations must take the points per service; to keep the old behaviour, check that the
      sum of the points is zero.
    - `ChillInactiveThreshold` has no default anymore. While it is not set, `chill_inactive` fails
      with `ChillInactiveDisabled`. Removing it through `set_staking_configs` disables the call.
    - `set_staking_configs` rejects a `chill_inactive_threshold` for which the weight of
      `chill_inactive` does not fit in one normal extrinsic.

    The weight of `chill_inactive` now includes reading `ErasRewardPointsByService` of every proof
    era. Its benchmark now writes different reward points for every era and service. Before, equal
    values were held only once in the proof, so the proof size did not grow with the number of
    eras.
crates:
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
